  "notes": "Source: official FDU program page https://www.fdu.edu/program/bs-computer-science-metro/ (Bachelor of Science in Computer Science, Metropolitan Campus, Teaneck, NJ; GHSE; ABET Computing Accreditation Commission accredited), whose full 8-semester Degree Plan was retrieved 2026-09-30. Cross-checked against the FDU Undergraduate Bulletin 2025-2026 (portal.fdu.edu/bulletin-archive, 'University Bulletin 2025-2026 11-03-2025.pdf'), which contains an archived copy of the identical page (retrieved 11/03/2025) with the IDENTICAL Degree Plan - no differences found, so catalog_year is 2025-2026. Transcription: course titles copied verbatim from the official Degree Plan; per-course credits confirmed from credit mentions in the bulletin text (e.g. CSCI1201 (3), MATH1201 (4), PHYS2201 (1), UNIV1001 (1), CSCI4386 (2), CSCI4384 (1), all five cybersecurity concentration courses (3 each)). CSCI3240's credit is not stated per-course in the bulletin; it is arithmetically forced to 3 credits by the published 5th-semester total of 15 (3+3+3+3 for the other four items). CSCI4384 = 1 credit forced by the 7th-semester total of 16. Semester totals 14/14/16/16/15/15/16/14 sum to exactly 120 = the catalog's published minimum ('A minimum of 120 credits is required for the BS in computer science degree'), so no discrepancy. Students must complete one of three concentrations (15 credits / 5 courses): the five choice slots default to the Cybersecurity and Information Assurance option set; alternates (Big Data Analytics; Game and Mobile Application Development) are listed in each slot's choice_note. Per the bulletin, UNIV1001/UNIV1002 may be waived for transfer students. Cooperative education option can earn 6 credits toward technical electives. This is the Metro/Teaneck ABET-accredited program; FDU also runs a separate non-ABET CS program at Florham (Maxwell Becton College) - NOT this plan. Florham/MS 4+1 variants were not mixed in.",
